inal number. If we're correct, we should get zero.\n\n$$\n(-40)+40=-40+40=0\\,✓\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445911 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445904 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445911 #edb/ref 1069 "q-68884" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445911 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445911 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the additive inverse of $-82?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445911 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d1ca34c0-e607-5050-a46f-b9f14c2f4fa4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445911 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the additive inverse of the number $-82$, we change its sign by placing a minus symbol $(-)$ in front of it. So, we obtain \n\n$$\n-\\,(-82)=82.\n$$\n\nTo check our work, we simply add the inverse to the original number. If we're correct, we should get zero.\n\n$$\n(-82)+82=-82+82=0\\,✓\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445912 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445899 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445912 #edb/ref 1069 "q-171110" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445912 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445912 #edb/ref 1071 "$23\\,+$$($\n{{field-1}}\n$)=0$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445912 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "de0a6181-6738-5d17-97f1-3a34c3d50cc1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445912 #edb/ref 1074 "The number that can be added to $23$ to give $0$ is the additive inverse of $23.$\n\nTo find the additive inverse of the number $23$, we change its sign by placing a minus symbol $(-)$ in front of it. So, we obtain \n\n$$\n-\\,(23)=-23.\n$$\n\nTo check our work, we simply add the inverse to the original number. If we're correct, we should get zero.\n\n$$\n23+(-23)=23-23=0\\,✓\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
